/T (AI agents are increasingly used in real-world workflows, but many teams still rely on manual and inconsistent testing methods. As a result, critical issues such as hallucinations, unsafe responses, prompt injection, tool misuse, and regressions may go undetected before deployment. This creates a need for a structured framework that can systematically evaluate agent safety, reliability, and release readiness.)
